# Fleet optimization W4b: the runner reads verdicts where critics post them and reads the real free memory. Issues 90 and 91. Tier C, at most two critic rounds, targeted tests. 2026-09-14
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/dev-agents.git wave-plans/dev-agents/2026-09-14-w4b-runner-truth.plan --detach --retries 1
# TIER: C
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | web-frontend | Branch feat/w4b-runner-truth from origin/main, in scripts/queue_loop.py and its tests only. Read issues 90 and 91 first. ONE, issue 90: a plan may carry a VERDICTS: header naming where its critics post (for example VERDICTS: Arlencho/olympus-platform#2340); the runner reads critic verdicts from the PR and from that issue, keeping only comments at or after the run start whose body names the PR number or the branch; no header keeps todays behaviour. TWO, issue 91: the memory guard reads the system-wide free percentage the way memory_pressure reports it (or free plus inactive plus speculative plus purgeable pages from vm_stat when that tool is absent), keeps swap used as the second condition, and keeps the existing unreadable-sensor and garbage-value rules. Tests with fixtures: an olympus-platform plan whose verdicts sit on the tracking issue lands as not silent; a comment on the issue for another PR is ignored; the memory_pressure output from 2026-09-14 02:58 (47 percent) with vm_stat raw free 23 percent reads as 47 and does not hold. VERIFY: tests/run-queue-loop-tests.sh only, real exit code in the PR body; no full suite. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR titled Fleet optimization W4b: verdict source and memory truth, Closes 90, Closes 91. | feat/w4b-runner-truth

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch feat/w4b-runner-truth. Tier C, round 1 of at most 2. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. Check that a verdict on the tracking issue for a different PR can never count, that an old verdict from before the run cannot count, and that the memory reading agrees with memory_pressure within two points on this machine at review time. Report only findings that make the runner land, hold or stop on a wrong reading. Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC W4B RUNNER TRUTH with SAFE-TO-MERGE, BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/w4b-runner-truth
